Here is a startup pitch for Tipperary, a new app that helps people find the average tip size for each restaurant:

```
{
  "Startup Pitch": {
    "Introduction": {
      "Problem Statement": "Tipping can be a daunting task, especially when dining out at a new restaurant. How much should you tip? Is 15% enough? 20%? More? The uncertainty can be frustrating and even lead to awkwardness at the table.",
      "Solution Overview": "Introducing Tipperary, the app that takes the guesswork out of tipping. With Tipperary, users can easily find the average tip size for each restaurant, ensuring they leave a fair and respectful gratuity every time."
    },
    "Market Opportunity": {
      "Market Size": "The US restaurant industry generates over $800 billion in annual sales, with an estimated 20% of that going towards tips. That's a $160 billion market, ripe for disruption.",
      "Target Audience": "Foodies, frequent diners, and anyone who's ever struggled with tipping will love Tipperary. Our initial target audience is millennials and Gen Z, who are more likely to dine out and use mobile apps to inform their decisions."
    },
    "Key Features": {
      "Restaurant Database": "Tipperary's comprehensive database features over 100,000 restaurants across the US, with average tip sizes crowdsourced from our user community.",
      "Personalized Recommendations": "Users can input their dining preferences and budget to receive personalized tip recommendations for each restaurant.",
      "Real-time Updates": "Our app updates in real-time, ensuring users have access to the most accurate and up-to-date tipping information."
    },
    "Competitive Advantage": {
      "Unique Selling Proposition": "Tipperary is the only app that provides average tip sizes for each restaurant, making it an indispensable tool for diners.",
      "Competitive Landscape": "Existing apps focus on restaurant reviews or reservations, but none provide tipping guidance. Tipperary fills this gap, offering a unique value proposition that sets us apart."
    },
    "Business Model": {
      "Revenue Streams": "Tipperary generates revenue through affiliate partnerships with restaurants, targeted advertising, and premium features for power users.",
      "Growth Strategy": "We'll leverage social media, influencer partnerships, and strategic restaurant partnerships to drive user acquisition and growth."
    },
    "Traction and Roadmap": {
      "Prototype": "Our functional prototype is complete, with a user-friendly interface and robust database.",
      "Launch Timeline": "We're on track to launch Tipperary in Q2 2023, with a phased rollout across major US cities.",
      "Future Development": "Post-launch, we'll focus on expanding our database, enhancing user features, and exploring integrations with popular food delivery and reservation platforms."
    },
    "Team": {
      "Founders": "Our team consists of experienced entrepreneurs, developers, and marketing experts, all passionate about solving the tipping dilemma.",
      "Advisors": "We're backed by a network of industry experts, including restaurateurs, food critics, and tech veterans."
    }
  }
}
```

